You will need 
- Docker Desktop Installed
- Docker Desktop running

2. Get the latest project
git clone "https://github.com/RADIANT-NOODLE/Group8Project.git"
cd Group8Project 
but if you already cloned it git pull is fine

3. Start Valora
Go to the backend folder  
run this command in your terminal:
    docker compose up -d --build
then wait for the containers to finish building.

4. Check Docker Desktop
You should see:
- valora_db
- valora_api
- valora_frontend

5. You can now open valora:
-Frontend:
http://localhost:4173

-Backend:
http://localhost:8000

-API documentation:
http://localhost:8000/docs


6. Test the actual system, create accounts and log in & out.
It should create actual records on the local PostgreSQL database and the login should return a JWT

